WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.380
You're saying I should hitch 
a ride on a hairball boat

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.480
and watch the Fire Festival? Me?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.730
You come up with some pretty
 impudent nonsense sometimes.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.420
Mom will treat us to 
chirashizushi and whatnot.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.490
Sushi made by a tanuki? 
The hair will get stuck in my throat!

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.700
At any rate, if you feel like it, please come to 
Tadasu no Mori tomorrow evening at 7 p.m.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.530
If I think of it, I might go. 
I might not.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.040
Wait, but don't count on me.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.190
He'll come.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.050
Imitating the various beauties 
of nature is refined and all,

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.680
but imitating humans is perhaps the most fun.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:50.330
Doing that, and enjoying ourselves at their
 events alongside them is strangely amusing.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.860
"It's a manifestation of our idiot blood."

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.700
Whenever we brothers got into some
 kind of mischief and caused a fuss

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.020
Dad would laugh and say that.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.540
One of the highlights of summer,
 the night of the Gozan Fire Festival.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:11.170
We tanuki matching the mood of the 
merry-making humans and making merry ourselves is

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:16.070
probably, in the end, another 
manifestation of our idiot blood.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.020
<b>Episode Four: 
Battle of the Daimonji Leisure Cruisers</b>

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.540
<b>Teakettle energy</b>

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.210
<b>For Prof. Akadama</b>

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.780
Is the professor really going to come?

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.590
Why don't you guys transform
 into Seven Lucky Gods, too?

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.160
Sorry Big Brother, I can't.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:35.820
Father would always transform 
into Hotei. In his remembra--

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:40.610
When someone tells us to transform, we stop 
wanting to transform. That's just how tanuki are,

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.890
Big Brother.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.330
Yo!

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.600
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.580
At this point there is no doubt Father
 is grieving in the afterlife again.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.600
As long as we're all smiling,
 Father must also be smiling.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.460
You're just thinking too hard
 and making things difficult.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.140
Look, here he is.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.850
Why isn't he coming over?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.910
What a piece of work.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.360
Hm? Oh, Professor!

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.680
If it isn't Yasaburo.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.520
What a coincidence! Are you taking a walk?

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.330
Indeed. It's a nice, cool evening.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.490
That's wonderful.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.350
By the way, Professor, are you aware 
that tonight is the Gozan Fire Festival?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.440
Oh, is it?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:06.140
We were just planning to use the inner 
parlor we borrowed from you to see the fires.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.640
If you're not in a hurry, how
 would you like to come with us?

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.100
It's not much, but we've 
prepared food and drink.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.960
Now that you mention it, you were saying 
something about that, weren't you.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.210
I was just thinking I'd like to take a break.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.510
I suppose it won't hurt 
to go for a little while.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.720
Is that Yaichiro? What's that look about?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.200
I'm abandoning formality this 
evening, Prof. Yakushibo.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.980
I like to have some fun now and then, too.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.190
By the way, when is Ben--

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.110
Professor, welcome!

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.370
It's such a waste to give 
it to the teakettle!

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.980
<b>For Prof. Akadama</b>

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.260
By the way, when is Ben--

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:37.040
Professor, over there is Mount 
Nyoigatake. Can you see Daimonji?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.210
That I can, I certainly can.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.810
By the way, when is Benten coming?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:00.730
<b>For Prof. Akadama</b>

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.730
<b>Teakettle energy</b>

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.720
She should know about the 
party today, so she might come.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.150
It's sure great that you're giving 
that darned teakettle so much to drink!

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.180
But Professor,

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.670
if we don't let the teakettle drink too, 
it'll get ornery and we'll fall.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.530
You hairballs might be
 in trouble if we fall, but--

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.280
Now, now Professor, don't be so stubborn.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.370
Don't get too close to the 
edge or you'll fall.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.340
I know!

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:30.900
The Ebisugawas are here.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.290
Look, there's Soun.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.290
Boom!

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.630
Those jerks, do they 
wanna go again this year?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.290
The Manpukumaru was an unfortunate accident.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.990
The fireworks they set off just happened 
to start a fire. Let's just say that.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.460
I'll do no such thing!

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:25.380
The Nise-emon election is coming
 up. Please don't cause trouble.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:29.330
Besides, relatives shouldn't 
squabble amongst themselves.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:40.600
Just dropping by.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.880
Oh, it's you.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:48.170
Well hello to you, too. Is some other 
tengu besides me supposed to come?

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.420
Shush.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.860
Welcome, nice to see you.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.060
How dull! So this is what it's 
like to see it from below.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.980
You don't want to go back there?

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.750
At this point I don't care. 
It would only mean more trouble.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:16.540
The False Nyoigatake Incident was 
really something, huh.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:21.830
Shimogamo Soichiro, now he was a real tanuki.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.170
It's been a long time since then, huh.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:29.220
I guess it was right around the time
 Shimogamo Yasaburo was born.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.800
I was a hairball the size of dandelion fluff.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:36.280
Soichiro was already 
Nise-emon by then, I think?

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:41.020
Yes, he was the chief keeping 
peace in Kyoto tanuki society.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.350
<b>Atago Jinja</b>

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:44.910
The start of the the whole incident

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:49.540
was a fight between Nyoigatake 
Yakushibo, here, and the Kurama tengu.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.390
Those bumpkins were trying to act cool.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:16.310
After making a total mess of the mountain, 
both Yakushibo and the Kurama tengu

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:20.070
got a good scolding from Atagoyama Tarobo.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:24.350
The Kurama tengu whipped 
up tengu winds first.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:30.730
You went and picked an unnecessary fight, 
so it ended up being awful later on.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.040
Later on?

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:36.110
Those Kurama tengu who were 
the root of the quarrel

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.760
took turns creeping onto Mount Nyoigatake

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:47.620
and throwing "Give Yakushibo Hell"
 parties day in, day out, tormenting him.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:04.460
And who was it who could not bear to see 
Yakushibo suffer like that and stood up for him?

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:08.460
The tanuki, Shimogamo Soichiro.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:11.740
Finally, reduced to state of pure
 instinctive fear, the Kurama tengu

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:14.290
prostrated themselves before 
Yakushibo and apologized.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.250
In a feat of extraordinary magnificence,

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:24.550
the tanuki Soichiro had transformed into 
Mount Nyoigatake itself for an entire week.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.340
That's where the name "False Nyoigatake 
Incident" comes from.

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:32.350
Father was really amazing, huh!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.330
He was quite a fool, yes.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:53.960
Lazily sleeping your days away, 
tanuki sure have it easy.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.960
I've gone and done something a bit foolish.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:03.920
It was terribly entertaining, 
but rather too much excitement.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.890
You shouldn't push yourself. Take care.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.110
Thank you.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.500
Benten is on the boat over there...

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:04.770
Why! Why is she not in the 
inner parlor I gave her

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.560
but on a boat with those damned hairballs?!

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.610
Why won't she stay at my side?

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.200
I don't know.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.310
They always go overboard.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.750
I'm going to go protest to Uncle.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.090
Shut up!

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.980
Mother, please have some patience.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:46.650
Dammit, they're always making fools of us!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.150
We absolutely cannot get involved!

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:50.930
There will be all kinds of troub--

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:58.760
Right in the middle there 
is good! Take precise aim!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.680
What are you doing just standing around?!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:15.750
Yashiro!

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:16.400
Right!

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:19.810
How can you do that?!

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.740
True forbearance is 
tolerating the intolerable!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.030
You're goin' to hell!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.140
It's about time we got outta here.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.400
Whoa, if I'd been hit I would've died!

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:08.400
There we go, now reel'er in.

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:13.860
Enemies in the same boat! 
Enemies in the same boat!

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:18.200
There are only a handful of'em! Move in 
real close and fire everything we've got!

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.640
Isn't there anything we can use?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.130
No, why would there be?!

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:50.460
Bring out the heir, Yaichiro.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.380
That's not the heir, it's the third son.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.370
What happened to Yaichiro? Is he curled 
up in a ball in the back of the room?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.890
"You will have heard of me by now,
 and here I am, before your eyes:"

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:12.710
the third son of Shimogamo 
Soichiro, Yasaburo!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.990
We know all that!

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.850
We're saying to hurry up and 
bring out that big brother of yours.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:21.000
We gotta thank him for biting 
our asses the other day, too.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.680
My butt nearly got an extra crack!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:28.670
By the way, Yasaburo, it's impossible
 to persist in calling that a leisure cruiser.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.460
That's not a boat, it's a tearoom!

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.380
Although it is the tanuki way 
 to do things flamboyantly,

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.400
moderation is surely vital.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.380
As a tanuki who upholds
 the teachings of my father

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.250
and lives purely and justly 
in this era of peace and tranquility

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:48.320
there is no doubt it is my 
duty to punish inexcusable tanuki

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.340
who ruined what should
 have been an enjoyable event.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.510
Are you okay?

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:59.680
Who cares? Just go for it.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:11.580
Well then, Uncle, I wish you well!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.020
Farewell, Ebisugawa!

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:47.700
Isn't it grand to be left to the wind
 and fall wherever it may take you?

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:54.720
Tanuki are truly idiots beyond saving.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.860
All right, let's take a 
photo in commemoration.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:09.540
What a great family!
 I'm sure your father is proud.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.100
The fuel is...!

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:22.840
Gone!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:24.610
It's gone!

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:25.350
None here!

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.710
How can this be?!

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.980
At this rate instead of being 
Nise-emon I'll end up a ruined tanuki!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.540
If we had even just a little Port wine...

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:46.700
Professor, that's--

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.160
Why should I have to
 go without my crucial Port wine

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:54.600
for the sake of that blasted teakettle?!

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:58.020
I am this evening's special guest!

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.430
I'm greater than tanuki! 
Greater than that teakettle!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.540
I will drink as much as I 
want, of what I want!

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:12.410
What is flying one's imagination freely 
through the sky if not the tengu's natural right?!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.770
I am Nyoigatake Yakushibo!

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.710
Owowow...

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:46.550
Are you okay?

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:52.220
I'm so sorry, there was no way
 I could've taken three of you.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:56.690
I'm all right, but... where's the professor?

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:06.020
But... this is no good.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:15.390
It's not here! Or here! Or here!

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:17.030
What's not?

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.970
The Fujin Raijin folding fan!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.900
I like you so much I want to eat you up.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:36.600
If she actually liked me that would be great.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.270
But I'm extremely reluctant to be eaten.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.230
When all else fails, retreat!

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:49.950
Being the resourceful guy
 that I am, I fled with so much skill

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:53.980
that from the end of summer into autumn,

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:58.630
I became renowned throughout
 Kyoto as "Yasaburo the Fugitive."

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:33.640
Even if you say, "The moon sure looks nice,"

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.580
my reply on full moon nights 
will always be the same.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:39.530
In that case, come with me!

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>The Friday Fellows</b>
